# Hooks → app

```
claude ─(hook stdin JSON)→ warroom-hook ─(Unix socket, 1 line)→ ingress.rs → IncomingSignal
       → WarRoomService::ingest → ClaudeProvider::translate → SessionEvent (+ extra) → commit
```

## Bridge invariants (crates/hook-bridge/src/main.rs) — never break these

- **Exit 0 always, in milliseconds when the app is down** (connect fails → exit). A slow or failing
  hook degrades every Claude session on the machine.
- **stdout only carries an explicit app decision** (PermissionRequest reply). Anything else printed
  is interpreted by Claude.
- It walks `/proc` from its parent upward: hooks may run through a shell, so `getppid()` is not the
  agent. The chain gives the agent PID (liveness) and the terminal/IDE (focus).
- Env hints captured at hook time: `TMUX`, `TMUX_PANE`, `TERM_PROGRAM`, `WARP_FOCUS_URL`, `AWR_PTY_ID`
  (set by our own PTYs). Plus `/proc/<agent>/cmdline` for the launch command.

## Socket protocol (crates/wire)

One connection per hook, one JSON line (`HookEnvelope`, `v: 1`). If `expects_reply`, the bridge keeps
the connection open and waits for a `HookReply` line; the app answering is how approvals work. Old
bridges sent no newline — ingress reads to newline **or** EOF. Socket:
`$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/agent-war-room/ingress.sock` (dir 0700; paths must stay < 108 bytes).

## Mapping (provider.rs)

Each hook → one `SessionEventKind` (+ `extra` events: a `/skill` prompt is also a `SkillInvoked`;
a `Skill` tool call too). Question tools (`AskUserQuestion`, `ExitPlanMode`) are `AwaitingYou`.
Tools with `agent_id` belong to a subagent. Unknown hooks → `Ok(None)` (ignored, not an error).

